  "body": "#1198 slice (b): move handles with drag-to-move. Slice (a), the bottom bar, merged in #1203.\n\n**GUI hand check needed.** The handles, the drag feel and the readout were tested only through the kittest harness and headless state tests. Nobody has looked at them on screen yet.\n\n## What changed\n- **Move mode in the bottom bar.** A seventh bar button (a four-armed cross) turns `State::move_handles` on and off. It is off by default, it is view state like pick-through, and it queues no command.\n- **Handles** (`crates/ui/src/move_drag.rs`, painted by `crates/ui/src/egui_app/move_handles.rs`). With Move on and exactly one shown part selected, three arms in the axis colours start at the part's bounding-box centre and each ends in a ball. The arms stay 70 px long on screen at any zoom. The ball under the pointer is drawn larger.\n- **Drag.** Pressing a ball takes the press before orbit and pick. Empty space still orbits. While the button is down, the preview slides the body along the axis (`world.rs` draws it offset) and never writes the world. The signed distance shows just above the bar. The distance is where the cursor ray comes closest to the axis line, so the part stays under the cursor in perspective and in ortho.\n- **One command per drag.** The release queues `CommandKind::MoveModelBy { name, delta }`. The drain (`crates/ui/src/state_move_by.rs`) runs it as the Model page's own `MoveModel::new`, with the rotation copied bit for bit. That means one undo step, the same staleness, the same following stock and the same fixture-clash warning as a typed move. No new placement path.\n- **What adds no history step:** Escape during a drag (the key is consumed), a drag that ends where it began, and turning Move off.\n- **Turned setups.** When the active setup holds the part turned (#326), the drag happens in that setup's frame. The shown delta is rotated back into the document frame, so the part moves along the axis the user sees.\n- Decisions are in `docs/decisions/1198-drag-to-move.md`: only parts are dragged in this slice, Move mode is off by default, and the preview moves the body only.\n\n## MCP\nNo new app command, so no new MCP tool. `MoveModelBy` is a UI queue verb over the existing `MoveModel`, and the MCP `move_model` tool already places a part through `MoveModel`. An agent can make every move a drag makes.\n\n## How tested\n- `egui_app::tests::body_drag` (kittest, the real shell; 5 tests):\n  - `handles_show_only_in_move_mode_on_a_selected_part`: a ball per axis, constant size when zoomed out, gone when Move is off.\n  - `a_ball_drag_is_one_undoable_move_by_the_dragged_distance`: the preview never writes the world; the release moves the part by the dragged distance along X only; one undo returns the history to clean.\n  - `escape_mid_drag_cancels_with_no_history_step`\n  - `a_drag_that_ends_where_it_began_adds_nothing`: also checks that a press on a ball is not a pick.\n  - `empty_space_still_orbits_in_move_mode`\n- `move_drag_tests` (headless state; 5 tests):\n  - `the_drag_distance_is_the_axis_point_under_the_cursor`: 12.5 mm along Y; one queued command.\n  - `a_press_off_the_balls_is_not_a_drag`\n  - `a_turned_setup_moves_the_part_along_the_axis_it_shows`\n  - `the_rotation_is_kept_bit_for_bit`\n  - `a_non_finite_distance_is_refused_by_name`\n- The existing bar laws hold with the seventh button: `viewport_bar::tests::bar_fits_its_buttons` and `law_tests::view_cube_tests::the_hud_is_laid_out_from_the_pane_alone`, which iterates every button in `NAVS`.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): ui lib plus the boundary, boundary_picks, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell and theme_files suites. 752 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The handles have not been seen on a real screen, and real mouse input has not been tried. GUI hand check needed.\n- The bar is wider now, so the viewport pixel goldens differ. They are regenerated at the cut; no PNG is changed here.\n- Fixtures and the stock are not draggable (recorded decision).\n\n## Left on #1198\n- (c) rotate handles.\n- (d) snapping with a modifier key, and typed values in the bar.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; upstream/main merged into the branch.\n\nChangelog: Viewport: a Move button in the bottom bar puts axis handles on the selected part; dragging a ball moves the part along that axis, one undo step per drag (#1198 b)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1198\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
